{{also|levant}}
==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|fr|en}} {{term|levant||[[rising]], sun's point of rising|lang=fr}}, form of {{term|lever||to rise|lang=fr}}, from {{etyl|la|en}} {{m|la|levō||to rise}} (cf. also Latin {{m|la|levans}}), from {{term|levis||light, not heavy|lang=la}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{rhymes|ænt|lang=en}}

===Proper noun===
{{en-proper noun}}

# The countries bordering the eastern [[Mediterranean Sea]], namely [[Syria]], [[Lebanon]], [[Israel]], [[Palestine]], [[Jordan]] and [[Cyprus]] (and sometimes also including [[Turkey]] and [[Egypt]]).
# An [[easterly]] wind, generally in the western Mediterranean Sea

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|wind}} [[levanter]]

====Antonyms====
* [[Maghreb]] <!-- western Mediterranean, literally “where the sun sets” -->

